WEBVTT

00:00:00.405 --> 00:00:02.977
You fill in a few fields and a finished

00:00:03.038 --> 00:00:06.107
file comes out, with the fonts, the

00:00:06.190 --> 00:00:09.002
colours and the layout already decided on

00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:10.894
your own device.

00:00:11.677 --> 00:00:14.308
You ship in minutes and it looks like you

00:00:14.368 --> 00:00:17.459
spent hours, and because the brand rules

00:00:17.538 --> 00:00:20.349
are baked into the tool, it is never your

00:00:20.409 --> 00:00:22.895
name on the off-brand file.

00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:26.469
Pick the lane below that matches what you

00:00:26.529 --> 00:00:28.294
are doing today.

00:00:29.084 --> 00:00:32.325
You are one hand in a relay: a developer

00:00:32.387 --> 00:00:35.559
can scale the tool you use into a pipeline

00:00:35.649 --> 00:00:39.194
and a colleague can run it self-serve, so

00:00:39.253 --> 00:00:42.089
The lifecycle of a campaign follows one

00:00:42.165 --> 00:00:45.319
asset through all three pairs of hands.

00:00:46.119 --> 00:00:47.556
New here?

00:00:48.337 --> 00:00:51.144
Start with Make something in 60 seconds

00:00:51.209 --> 00:00:53.671
and come back once you know which part you

00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:55.795
want to go deeper on.

00:00:56.553 --> 00:01:00.048
Questions & answers covers what people ask

00:01:00.110 --> 00:01:02.893
before they trust a free tool.

00:01:03.669 --> 00:01:06.581
How Lolly compares is the honest account

00:01:06.619 --> 00:01:10.044
of what to reach for something else for.

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:11.900
Make

00:01:12.844 --> 00:01:15.477
Pick a tool, fill in a few fields and

00:01:15.539 --> 00:01:17.944
download the finished file.

00:01:18.705 --> 00:01:21.707
Or open the Design canvas and lay it out

00:01:21.794 --> 00:01:25.017
freehand: either way the colours, the type

00:01:25.075 --> 00:01:27.341
and the spacing come from your brand

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:30.229
rather than from memory, and nothing needs

00:01:30.267 --> 00:01:31.645
an account.

